    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `other`: the candidate subset; borrowed, never modified.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## `true` when `self` is a superset of `other`, `false` otherwise. Reads only.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var a as SetInt is calling new_set_int
    ## var b as SetInt is calling new_set_int
    ## calling a.add with 1
    ## calling b.add with 1
    ## var sup as bool is calling a.is_superset with b    # true
    ## ```
    weave is_superset with other as SetInt into bool:
        return calling other.is_subset with (essence of self)

    ## Returns true if `self` and `other` have no elements in common.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `other`: the second set; borrowed, never modified.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## `true` when the sets are disjoint, `false` otherwise. Reads only.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var a as SetInt is calling new_set_int
    ## var b as SetInt is calling new_set_int
    ## calling a.add with 1
    ## calling b.add with 2
    ## var d as bool is calling a.is_disjoint with b    # true
    ## ```
    weave is_disjoint with other as SetInt into bool:
        for k in self->items:
            if calling other.items.contains with k:
                return false
        return true

    ## Returns true if `self` and `other` contain exactly the same set of
    ## elements.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `other`: the set to compare against; borrowed, never modified.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## `true` when both sets have the same members, `false` otherwise. Reads
    ## only; the insertion order is irrelevant.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var a as SetInt is calling new_set_int
    ## var b as SetInt is calling new_set_int
    ## calling a.add with 1
    ## calling b.add with 1
    ## var same as bool is calling a.equals with b    # true
    ## ```
    weave equals with other as SetInt into bool:
        if (calling self.len) != (calling other.len):
            return false
        return calling self.is_subset with other

    ## Returns a fresh independent copy of `self`.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - None: the receiver is copied.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## An owned fresh `SetInt`. Release its backing map with `banish c.items`.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var s as SetInt is calling new_set_int
    ## calling s.add with 1
    ## var c as SetInt is calling s.clone
    ## ```
    weave clone into SetInt:
        var result as SetInt is calling new_set_int
        for k in self->items:
            calling result.items.put with k, 1
        return result

    ## Returns a fresh list containing all parsed integer elements of `self`.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - None: the receiver is listed.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## An owned fresh `list of int`; release it with `banish`. Order is hash
    ## order, not insertion order.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var s as SetInt is calling new_set_int
    ## calling s.add with 7
    ## var xs as list of int is calling s.to_list_int
    ## ```
    weave to_list_int into list of int:
        var result as list of int is list of int
        for k in self->items:
            calling result.push with k
        return result

    ## Returns the arithmetic sum of all integers in `self`. Returns 0 if empty.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - None: the receiver is reduced.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## The sum as an `int`; the empty set collapses to the identity `0`.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var s as SetInt is calling new_set_int
    ## calling s.add with 2
    ## calling s.add with 3
    ## var total as int is calling s.sum_ints    # 5
    ## ```
    weave sum_ints into int:
        var total as int is 0
        for k in self->items:
            set total is total + k
        return total

    ## Returns the minimum integer in `self`. Returns 0 if empty.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - None: the receiver is reduced.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## The smallest element as an `int`; the empty set collapses to `0`.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var s as SetInt is calling new_set_int
    ## calling s.add with 5
    ## calling s.add with -2
    ## var lo as int is calling s.min_int    # -2
    ## ```
    weave min_int into int:
        var n as int is calling self.len
        if n == 0:
            return 0
        var first as bool is true
        var lo as int is 0
        for k in self->items:
            if first:
                set lo is k
                set first is false
            else:
                if k < lo:
                    set lo is k
        return lo

    ## Returns the maximum integer in `self`. Returns 0 if empty.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - None: the receiver is reduced.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## The largest element as an `int`; the empty set collapses to `0`.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var s as SetInt is calling new_set_int
    ## calling s.add with 5
    ## calling s.add with 9
    ## var hi as int is calling s.max_int    # 9
    ## ```
    weave max_int into int:
        var n as int is calling self.len
        if n == 0:
            return 0
        var first as bool is true
        var hi as int is 0
        for k in self->items:
            if first:
                set hi is k
                set first is false
            else:
                if k > hi:
                    set hi is k
        return hi

    ## Converts this `SetInt` to an equivalent `SetString` with stringified
    ## keys.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - None: the receiver is converted.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## An owned fresh `SetString`. Unlike every other set-returning method, this
    ## one **owns its keys**: each key is a fresh interpolation whose buffer is
    ## handed to the result, so release it with `release`, **not**
    ## `banish t.items` (which would leak the key buffers).
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## One owned key buffer per element. Free them, and then the map, with
    ## `calling t.release`.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var s as SetInt is calling new_set_int
    ## calling s.add with 7
    ## var t as SetString is calling s.to_set_string
    ## calling t.release
    ## ```
    weave to_set_string into SetString:
        var result as SetString is calling new_set_string
        for k in self->items:
            let s as string is "{k}"
            calling result._put_owned with s
        return result

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generic Set enchanting methods
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

enchanting Set shard T:
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # Note: no generic `ritual` constructor
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # A type-qualified generic ritual (`Set.empty of T`) miscompiles or misbinds
    # as soon as the bundle holds more than one `Set of T` specialisation, which
    # is always the case for this module (its own tests instantiate several).
    # Element types are therefore built with the generic module functions
    # `make_set shard T` / `from_items_set shard T` or with the concrete
    # constructors (`new_int_set`, ...); see the module design notes.

    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # Instance methods
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------

    ## Inserts `item` into the set, **borrowing** it. Inserting an element already
    ## present is a no-op, because a set stores each element at most once.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `item`: the element to insert. Only its key header is copied into the
    ##   backing map, never the payload it points at.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## Nothing; the method returns `void` and mutates the receiver in place.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## **`item` must outlive the set.** That is invisible for a plain value type
    ## (`int`, `float`, `char`, `bool`, a POD rune), but a `string`, `list`, `map`
    ## or heap-owning rune element aliases the caller's buffer: releasing it while
    ## the set still holds it leaves a dangling key. See the `Set shard T` memory
    ## note for why there is no `add_owned` here.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var s as Set of int is calling new_int_set
    ## calling s.add with 7
    ## ```
    weave add with item as T into void:
        calling self->items.put with item, 1

    ## Returns true when `item` is currently a member of the set.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `item`: the element to look up; borrowed, never modified.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## `true` when the set holds `item`, `false` otherwise. Reads only.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var s as Set of int is calling new_int_set
    ## calling s.add with 7
    ## var found as bool is calling s.contains with 7    # true
    ## ```
    weave contains with item as T into bool:
        return calling self->items.contains with item

    ## Removes `item` from the set. Returns true when it was present (and has
    ## been removed); returns false when the set did not contain it.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `item`: the element to remove; borrowed, never modified.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## `true` when the element was present and has been removed, `false` when it
    ## was absent.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var s as Set of int is calling new_int_set
    ## calling s.add with 7
    ## var removed as bool is calling s.remove with 7    # true
    ## ```
    weave remove with item as T into bool:
        return calling self->items.remove with item

    ## Returns the number of distinct elements currently stored in the set.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - None: the receiver is measured.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## The element count as an `int`. Reads only.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var s as Set of int is calling new_int_set
    ## calling s.add with 7
    ## var n as int is calling s.len    # 1
    ## ```
    weave len into int:
        return calling self->items.len

    ## Removes every element, leaving the set empty.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - None.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## Nothing; the method returns `void` and mutates the receiver in place.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var s as Set of int is calling new_int_set
    ## calling s.add with 7
    ## calling s.clear
    ## ```
    weave clear into void:
        calling self->items.clear

    ## Returns true when the set holds no elements at all.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - None: the receiver is inspected.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## `true` for an empty set, `false` otherwise. Reads only.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var s as Set of int is calling new_int_set
    ## var empty as bool is calling s.is_empty    # true
    ## ```
    weave is_empty into bool:
        return calling self->items.is_empty

    ## Returns a fresh `Set of T` containing every element present in `self` or
    ## `other`.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `other`: the second set; borrowed, never modified or released.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## An owned fresh `Set of T`. Release its backing map with `banish u.items`.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var a as Set of int is calling new_int_set
    ## var b as Set of int is calling new_int_set
    ## calling a.add with 1
    ## calling b.add with 2
    ## var u as Set of int is calling a.union with b
    ## ```
    weave union with other as Set of T into Set of T:
        var result as Set of T with:
            set .items is map of T to int
        for k in self->items:
            calling result.items.put with k, 1
        for k in other.items:
            calling result.items.put with k, 1
        return result

    ## Returns a fresh `Set of T` containing only elements present in both
    ## `self` and `other`.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `other`: the second set; borrowed, never modified or released.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## An owned fresh `Set of T`. Release its backing map with `banish i.items`.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var a as Set of int is calling new_int_set
    ## var b as Set of int is calling new_int_set
    ## calling a.add with 1
    ## calling b.add with 1
    ## var i as Set of int is calling a.intersect with b
    ## ```
    weave intersect with other as Set of T into Set of T:
        var result as Set of T with:
            set .items is map of T to int
        for k in self->items:
            if calling other.items.contains with k:
                calling result.items.put with k, 1
        return result

    ## Returns a fresh `Set of T` with elements present in `self` but absent from
    ## `other`.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `other`: the second set; borrowed, never modified or released.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## An owned fresh `Set of T`. Release its backing map with `banish d.items`.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var a as Set of int is calling new_int_set
    ## var b as Set of int is calling new_int_set
    ## calling a.add with 1
    ## var d as Set of int is calling a.difference with b
    ## ```
    weave difference with other as Set of T into Set of T:
        var result as Set of T with:
            set .items is map of T to int
        for k in self->items:
            if (calling other.items.contains with k) == false:
                calling result.items.put with k, 1
        return result

    ## Returns a fresh `Set of T` with elements in either `self` or `other`, but
    ## not both.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `other`: the second set; borrowed, never modified or released.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## An owned fresh `Set of T`. Release its backing map with `banish x.items`.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var a as Set of int is calling new_int_set
    ## var b as Set of int is calling new_int_set
    ## calling a.add with 1
    ## calling b.add with 2
    ## var x as Set of int is calling a.symmetric_difference with b
    ## ```
    weave symmetric_difference with other as Set of T into Set of T:
        var result as Set of T with:
            set .items is map of T to int
        for k in self->items:
            if (calling other.items.contains with k) == false:
                calling result.items.put with k, 1
        for k in other.items:
            if (calling self->items.contains with k) == false:
                calling result.items.put with k, 1
        return result

    ## Returns true if every element in `self` is also present in `other`.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `other`: the candidate superset; borrowed, never modified.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## `true` when `self` is a subset of `other`, `false` otherwise. Reads only.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var a as Set of int is calling new_int_set
    ## var b as Set of int is calling new_int_set
    ## calling a.add with 1
    ## calling b.add with 1
    ## var sub as bool is calling a.is_subset with b    # true
    ## ```
    weave is_subset with other as Set of T into bool:
        for k in self->items:
            if (calling other.items.contains with k) == false:
                return false
        return true

    ## Returns true if every element in `other` is also present in `self`.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `other`: the candidate subset; borrowed, never modified.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## `true` when `self` is a superset of `other`, `false` otherwise. Reads only.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var a as Set of int is calling new_int_set
    ## var b as Set of int is calling new_int_set
    ## calling a.add with 1
    ## calling b.add with 1
    ## var sup as bool is calling a.is_superset with b    # true
    ## ```
    weave is_superset with other as Set of T into bool:
        for k in other.items:
            if (calling self->items.contains with k) == false:
                return false
        return true

    ## Returns true if `self` and `other` have no elements in common.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `other`: the second set; borrowed, never modified.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## `true` when the sets are disjoint, `false` otherwise. Reads only.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var a as Set of int is calling new_int_set
    ## var b as Set of int is calling new_int_set
    ## calling a.add with 1
    ## calling b.add with 2
    ## var d as bool is calling a.is_disjoint with b    # true
    ## ```
    weave is_disjoint with other as Set of T into bool:
        for k in self->items:
            if calling other.items.contains with k:
                return false
        return true

    ## Returns true if `self` and `other` contain exactly the same set of
    ## elements.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `other`: the set to compare against; borrowed, never modified.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## `true` when both sets have the same members, `false` otherwise. Reads
    ## only; the insertion order is irrelevant.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var a as Set of int is calling new_int_set
    ## var b as Set of int is calling new_int_set
    ## calling a.add with 1
    ## calling b.add with 1
    ## var same as bool is calling a.equals with b    # true
    ## ```
    weave equals with other as Set of T into bool:
        if (calling self->items.len) != (calling other.items.len):
            return false
        for k in self->items:
            if (calling other.items.contains with k) == false:
                return false
        return true

    ## Returns a fresh independent copy of `self`.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - None: the receiver is copied.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## An owned fresh `Set of T`. Release its backing map with `banish c.items`.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var s as Set of int is calling new_int_set
    ## calling s.add with 1
    ## var c as Set of int is calling s.clone
    ## ```
    weave clone into Set of T:
        var result as Set of T with:
            set .items is map of T to int
        for k in self->items:
            calling result.items.put with k, 1
        return result

    ## Returns a fresh list containing all elements of `self` in internal hash
    ## order.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - None: the receiver is listed.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## An owned fresh `list of T`; release it with `banish`. The order is hash
    ## order, not insertion order.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var s as Set of int is calling new_int_set
    ## calling s.add with 1
    ## var xs as list of int is calling s.to_list
    ## ```
    weave to_list into list of T:
        var out as list of T is list of T
        for k in self->items:
            calling out.push with k
        return out

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generic set constructors
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Creates an empty `Set of T`.
##
## `T` is named explicitly at the call site (`calling make_set of int`) because it
## cannot be inferred. Unlike a generic `ritual` constructor, this module
## function keeps working when the bundle holds several `Set of T`
## specialisations.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - None: the backing map is created empty.
##
## ## Retorno
## An owned empty `Set of T`. Release its backing map with `banish s.items`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var s as Set of int is calling make_set of int
## calling s.add with 7
## ```
weave make_set shard T into Set of T:
    var s as Set of T with:
        set .items is map of T to int
    return s

## Builds a `Set of T` from a list of `T`, automatically deduplicating items.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `items`: the source list; borrowed, never modified. `T` is named at the
##   call site.
##
## ## Retorno
## An owned `Set of T` holding each distinct element of `items` once. Release its
## backing map with `banish s.items`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var xs as list of int is [1, 1, 2]
## var s as Set of int is calling from_items_set of int with xs
## ```
weave from_items_set shard T with items as list of T into Set of T:
    var s as Set of T with:
        set .items is map of T to int
    for x in items:
        calling s.items.put with x, 1
    return s

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Concrete generic constructors
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Creates an empty `Set of int`.
##
## The concrete constructors spell the element type for the common cases; they
## and the generic module functions (`make_set`, `from_items_set`) are the
## supported way to start a generic set, because a type-qualified generic
## `ritual` constructor miscompiles (see the module design notes).
##
## ## Parámetros
## - None.
##
## ## Retorno
## An owned empty `Set of int`. Release its backing map with `banish s.items`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var s as Set of int is calling new_int_set
## calling s.add with 7
## ```
weave ritual new_int_set into Set of int:
    var s as Set of int with:
        set .items is map of int to int
    return s

## Creates an empty `Set of string`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - None.
##
## ## Retorno
## An owned empty `Set of string`. Release its backing map with `banish s.items`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var s as Set of string is calling new_string_set
## calling s.add with "ada"
## ```
weave ritual new_string_set into Set of string:
    var s as Set of string with:
        set .items is map of string to int
    return s

## Creates an empty `Set of float`.
